/-!
# Descent of the setoid condition along an fppf morphism of algebraic spaces

Let `𝒳 ⟶ 𝒵` and `𝒴 ⟶ 𝒵` be 1-morphisms of categories fibred in groupoids over the big fppf site
of a scheme `S`, with `𝒳` a stack. If `𝒴` and `𝒵` are represented by algebraic spaces `Y` and `Z`
over `S`, the morphism `a : Y ⟶ Z` associated to `𝒴 ⟶ 𝒵` is surjective, flat and locally of finite
presentation, and the 2-fibre product `𝒴 ×_𝒵 𝒳` is a stack in setoids, then `𝒳` is a stack in
setoids.

The geometric input is that such an `a` admits a section fppf-locally, and in fact over a *single*
morphism of the site: `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_singleton_fppf_lift`. Transported through the
chosen equivalences with categories of elements, that says every object of a fibre of `𝒵` is
locally in the essential image of `𝒴 ⟶ 𝒵` on fibres, which is exactly the hypothesis
`CategoryTheory.Functor.LocallyEssSurjOnFibers` of the general descent criterion
`CategoryTheory.Functor.isStackInSetoids_of_isThin_of_locallyEssSurj`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_singleton_fppf_lift`: a surjective, flat, locally finitely
  presented morphism of algebraic spaces over `S` admits a section over a single covering morphism
  of the site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isStackInSetoids_of_fppf_baseChange`: **Stacks 05XL**.

## Implementation notes

The hypothesis that `a` is *the* morphism of algebraic spaces associated to `𝒴 ⟶ 𝒵` is written as
the computation of `a` on every section named by an object
(`CategoryTheory.PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj`). That is the conclusion of Stacks 04SW,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.morphismSpaceEquiv_app_sectionOfObj`, so a consumer holding the
1-morphism discharges it from library material; and it is free of the heterogeneous equality that a
formulation in terms of the underlying objects of the categories of elements would carry, because
`sectionOfObj` takes the identification of the base as an argument.

That `𝒳` is a stack is a hypothesis, in the sieve-indexed sense of Stacks 026F
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStack`): it is the first conjunct of being a stack in groupoids, and it
is what `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStackInSetoids` contains. Nothing has to be proved about it, so
the conclusion is thinness of the fibres of `𝒳`, which is what the source's proof establishes.
The hypotheses that `𝒴` and `𝒵` are stacks are not needed: `𝒵` has thin fibres because it is
represented by a presheaf of sets, by
`CategoryTheory.PresheafOfCategories.isFiberedInSetoids_discreteProjection` transported along the
chosen equivalence, and the groupoid structure of all three fibres is part of being fibred in
groupoids.

Local essential surjectivity is produced over the sieve generated by the single morphism `j` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_singleton_fppf_lift`; over a member `h ≫ j` of that sieve the
required object of `𝒴` is the chosen pullback along `h` of the one over `j`, the comparison being
the chosen-pullback associativity
`CategoryTheory.Functor.pullbackFiberCompIso` composed with the 1-morphism's pullback comparison
`CategoryTheory.Functor.mapPullbackFiberIso'`.

The fppf-local section is got from the *atlas* of the fibre product `Y ×_{Z} T`, not from the
chart of a surjective morphism of Stacks 03MF, which this library does not have: the atlas is a
surjective étale morphism from a scheme by the definition of an algebraic space (Stacks 025Y), and
composing it with the projection — flat and locally of finite presentation by base change — gives
a morphism of the site which is surjective, flat and locally of finite presentation, hence an fppf
covering after refinement by Stacks 03WX.

The morphism universe of the three categories fibred in groupoids is that of the site, as in
`CategoryTheory.Functor.isStackInSetoids_of_isStackInSetoids_twoFibreProduct` (Stacks 05W9) and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.morphismSpaceEquiv_app_sectionOfObj` (Stacks 04SW); their object universe
is free.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05W9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05W9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05XL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05XL)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Functor CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/- The descent argument reasons about morphisms of the fibre categories of the structure functors
of categories fibred in groupoids. Those spellings are built from definitions the `implicit`
transparency level does not unfold -- `Functor.Fiber` and its inclusion and induced functors -- so
the goals are not type-correct at that level and `rw`, `simp` and `Trans` synthesis decline to act
on them. -/
attribute [local implicit_reducible] CategoryTheory.Functor.Fiber
  CategoryTheory.Functor.Fiber.fiberInclusion CategoryTheory.Functor.Fiber.mapOfComp

universe u w

/-! ### A section over a single covering morphism -/

namespace Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **A surjective, flat, locally finitely presented morphism of algebraic spaces over `S` has a
section over a single covering morphism of the site.** For every object `U` of the big fppf site of
`S` and every section `x` of the target over `U` there are a morphism `j : V ⟶ U` whose generated
sieve covers `U` and a section of the source over `V` whose image is the restriction of `x`.

The morphism `j` is the composite of the atlas of the fibre product `F ×_{x, G} U` with the
projection to `U`. -/
theorem exists_singleton_fppf_lift
    {F G : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u}
    (hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F) (hG : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS G) (a : F ⟶ G)
    (hsurj : IsSurjective B S hS a) (hflat : IsFlat B S hS a)
    (hlfp : IsLocallyOfFinitePresentation B S hS a)
    (U : BigFppfOver B S hS) (x : G.obj (op U)) :
    ∃ (V : BigFppfOver B S hS) (j : V ⟶ U),
      Sieve.generate (Presieve.singleton j) ∈ BigFppfOver.topology B S hS U ∧
      ∃ s : F.obj (op V), a.app (op V) s = G.map j.op x := by
  classical
  let Tscheme := BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS
  let ξ : yoneda.obj U ⟶ G := yonedaEquiv.symm x
  let p := pullback.fst ξ a
  have hP : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS (pullback ξ a) :=
    isAlgebraicSpace_pullback B S hS ξ a (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS U) hF hG
  let b : (⟨yoneda.obj U, isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS U⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) ⟶ ⟨G, hG⟩ :=
    ObjectProperty.homMk ξ
  let f : (⟨F, hF⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) ⟶ ⟨G, hG⟩ := ObjectProperty.homMk a
  have hpb := AlgebraicSpaces.isPullback_fiberProduct B S hS b f
  have hpflat : IsFlat B S hS p :=
    (isFlat_isStableUnderBaseChange B S hS).of_isPullback hpb.flip hflat
  have hplfp : IsLocallyOfFinitePresentation B S hS p :=
    (isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_isStableUnderBaseChange B S hS).of_isPullback hpb.flip hlfp
  have hpsurj : IsSurjective B S hS p := fun t ↦ by
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hsurj (pointsMap B S hS _ ξ t)
    obtain ⟨z, hz, _⟩ := exists_point_of_isPullback B S hS hpb t y hy.symm
    exact ⟨z, hz⟩
  obtain ⟨V, α, hαsurj, hαet⟩ := hP.exists_atlas
  have hαEtale : IsEtale B S hS α := chart_map_isEtale B S hS V α hαet
  let j : V ⟶ U := yoneda.preimage (α ≫ p)
  have hjmap : yoneda.map j = α ≫ p := yoneda.map_preimage _
  have hVsp : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS (yoneda.obj V) := isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS V
  have hUsp : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS (yoneda.obj U) := isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS U
  have hflatj : IsFlat B S hS (yoneda.map j) :=
    hjmap ▸ isFlat_comp B S hS hVsp hP hUsp α p (isFlat_atlas B S hS hP hαEtale) hpflat
  have hlfpj : IsLocallyOfFinitePresentation B S hS (yoneda.map j) :=
    hjmap ▸ isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_comp B S hS hVsp hP hUsp α p
      (isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_atlas B S hS hP hαEtale) hplfp
  have hsurjj : IsSurjective B S hS (yoneda.map j) :=
    hjmap ▸ isSurjective_comp B S hS
      ((surjective_iff_surjective_pointsMap B S hS _ hP V α).1 hαsurj) hpsurj
  have hjflat : Flat (Tscheme.map j) :=
    hflatj V U (𝟙 (yoneda.obj V)) (𝟙 (yoneda.obj U)) j
      (presheaf_etale_id B S hS V) (presheaf_etale_id B S hS U) (by simp)
  have hjlfp : LocallyOfFinitePresentation (Tscheme.map j) :=
    hlfpj V U (𝟙 (yoneda.obj V)) (𝟙 (yoneda.obj U)) j
      (presheaf_etale_id B S hS V) (presheaf_etale_id B S hS U) (by simp)
  have hjSurj : Surjective (Tscheme.map j) :=
    ((surjective_iff_surjective_pointsMap B S hS (yoneda.obj U) hUsp V (yoneda.map j)).2
      hsurjj).2 (𝟙 _) (𝟙 _) j (by simpa using IsPullback.of_id_fst (f := yoneda.map j))
  refine ⟨V, j, sieve_generate_singleton_mem_topology_over_of_flat B S hS j hjSurj hjflat hjlfp,
    (α ≫ pullback.snd ξ a).app (op V) (𝟙 V), ?_⟩
  have hl : (α ≫ pullback.snd ξ a) ≫ a = yoneda.map j ≫ ξ := by
    rw [Category.assoc, ← pullback.condition, ← Category.assoc, hjmap]
  simpa [ξ] using congrArg (fun t => t.app (op V) (𝟙 V)) hl

end Space

/-! ### The descent statement -/

namespace Stack

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- The chosen pullback of a fibre isomorphism along a morphism of the base. -/
private noncomputable def pullbackFiberMapIso {𝒞 : Type*} [Category 𝒞] {𝒟 : Type*} [Category 𝒟]
    {q : 𝒟 ⥤ 𝒞} [q.IsFibered] {U : 𝒞} {x y : q.Fiber U} (e : x ≅ y) {V : 𝒞} (g : V ⟶ U) :
    pullbackFiber q x g ≅ pullbackFiber q y g where
  hom := pullbackFiberHom e.hom g
  inv := pullbackFiberHom e.inv g
  hom_inv_id := by rw [← pullbackFiberHom_comp, e.hom_inv_id, pullbackFiberHom_id]
  inv_hom_id := by rw [← pullbackFiberHom_comp, e.inv_hom_id, pullbackFiberHom_id]

/-- **Stacks 05XL.** Let `𝒳 ⟶ 𝒵` and `𝒴 ⟶ 𝒵` be 1-morphisms of categories fibred in groupoids over
the big fppf site of `S`, with `𝒳` a stack. If `𝒴` and `𝒵` are represented by algebraic spaces `Y`
and `Z` over `S` through chosen equivalences over the site, the morphism `a : Y ⟶ Z` these
equivalences associate to `𝒴 ⟶ 𝒵` is surjective, flat and locally of finite presentation, and the
2-fibre product `𝒴 ×_𝒵 𝒳` is a stack in setoids, then `𝒳` is a stack in setoids. -/
@[stacks 05XL]
theorem isStackInSetoids_of_fppf_baseChange
    {𝒳 𝒴 𝒵 : CatFiberedInGroupoids.{u, u, u + 1, w} (BigFppfOver B S hS)}
    (f : 𝒳 ⟶ 𝒵) (g : 𝒴 ⟶ 𝒵)
    (h𝒳 : 𝒳.val.p.IsStack (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS))
    (Y Z : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u)
    (hY : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Y) (hZ : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Z)
    (eY : StacksRepresentableCFG.EquivalenceOver 𝒴.val.p
      (presheafOfCategories (Y ⋙ typeToCat)).p)
    (eZ : StacksRepresentableCFG.EquivalenceOver 𝒵.val.p
      (presheafOfCategories (Z ⋙ typeToCat)).p)
    (a : Y ⟶ Z)
    (ha : ∀ y : 𝒴.val.obj,
      a.app (op (𝒴.val.p.obj y)) (PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj eY y rfl) =
        PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj eZ ((CatFiberedInGroupoids.homFunctor g).obj y)
          (Functor.congr_obj (CatFiberedInGroupoids.homFunctor_comp_p g) y))
    (hsurj : Space.IsSurjective B S hS a) (hflat : Space.IsFlat B S hS a)
    (hlfp : Space.IsLocallyOfFinitePresentation B S hS a)
    (hP : (TwoFibreProductOver.structureFunctor 𝒴.val.p 𝒳.val.p 𝒵.val.p
        (CatFiberedInGroupoids.homFunctor g) (CatFiberedInGroupoids.homFunctor f)).IsStackInSetoids
      (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS)) :
    𝒳.val.p.IsStackInSetoids (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) := by
  classical
  let J := BigFppfOver.topology B S hS
  let Fg := CatFiberedInGroupoids.homFunctor g
  let hFg := CatFiberedInGroupoids.homFunctor_comp_p g
  have hgpdZ : 𝒵.val.p.IsFiberedInGroupoids := 𝒵.isFiberedInGroupoids
  have hgpdY : 𝒴.val.p.IsFiberedInGroupoids := 𝒴.isFiberedInGroupoids
  let : 𝒵.val.p.IsFibered := hgpdZ.isFibered
  let : 𝒴.val.p.IsFibered := hgpdY.isFibered
  have hZthin : ∀ V : BigFppfOver B S hS, Quiver.IsThin (𝒵.val.p.Fiber V) :=
    (StacksRepresentableCFG.isFiberedInSetoids_of_equivalenceOver eZ
      (PresheafOfCategories.isFiberedInSetoids_discreteProjection Z)).fiber_isThin
  have hGone : IsFibredOneMorphism 𝒴.val.p 𝒵.val.p Fg :=
    IsFibredOneMorphism.of_isFiberedInGroupoids hgpdZ hFg
  have hloc : LocallyEssSurjOnFibers hgpdZ.isFibered hFg J := by
    intro U x
    obtain ⟨V, j, hj, s, hs⟩ := Space.exists_singleton_fppf_lift B S hS hY hZ a hsurj hflat hlfp
      U (PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj eZ x.1 x.2)
    obtain ⟨z₀, hz₀, hz₀s⟩ := PresheafOfCategories.exists_sectionOfObj eY (W := V) s
    have hnames : PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj eZ
        ((Fiber.mapOfComp 𝒴.val.p 𝒵.val.p Fg hFg V).obj ⟨z₀, hz₀⟩).1
          ((Fiber.mapOfComp 𝒴.val.p 𝒵.val.p Fg hFg V).obj ⟨z₀, hz₀⟩).2 =
        PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj eZ (pullbackFiber 𝒵.val.p x j).1
          (pullbackFiber 𝒵.val.p x j).2 := by
      have hmap : PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj eZ (pullbackFiber 𝒵.val.p x j).1
          (pullbackFiber 𝒵.val.p x j).2 =
          Z.map j.op (PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj eZ x.1 x.2) :=
        PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj_map eZ x.2 (pullbackFiber 𝒵.val.p x j).2 j
          (IsPreFibered.pullbackMap x.2 j) inferInstance
      have hz : a.app (op V) (PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj eY z₀ hz₀) =
          PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj eZ (Fg.obj z₀)
            ((Functor.congr_obj hFg z₀).trans hz₀) := by
        obtain rfl : 𝒴.val.p.obj z₀ = V := hz₀
        exact ha z₀
      have hzF : PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj eZ
          ((Fiber.mapOfComp 𝒴.val.p 𝒵.val.p Fg hFg V).obj ⟨z₀, hz₀⟩).1
            ((Fiber.mapOfComp 𝒴.val.p 𝒵.val.p Fg hFg V).obj ⟨z₀, hz₀⟩).2 =
          PresheafOfCategories.sectionOfObj eZ (Fg.obj z₀)
            ((Functor.congr_obj hFg z₀).trans hz₀) := rfl
      rw [hzF, ← hz, hz₀s, hs, ← hmap]
    refine ⟨Sieve.generate (Presieve.singleton j), hj, ?_⟩
    rintro W gw ⟨W', h, e, ⟨⟩, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨pullbackFiber 𝒴.val.p ⟨z₀, hz₀⟩ h, ⟨(mapPullbackFiberIso' hGone ⟨z₀, hz₀⟩ h).symm ≪≫
      pullbackFiberMapIso (PresheafOfCategories.fiberIsoOfSectionOfObj_eq eZ
        ((Fiber.mapOfComp 𝒴.val.p 𝒵.val.p Fg hFg V).obj ⟨z₀, hz₀⟩).2
        (pullbackFiber 𝒵.val.p x j).2 hnames) h ≪≫
      pullbackFiberCompIso x j h⟩⟩
  exact isStackInSetoids_of_isThin_of_locallyEssSurj hFg
    (CatFiberedInGroupoids.homFunctor_comp_p f) hgpdZ hZthin 𝒳.isFiberedInGroupoids h𝒳 hloc hP

end Stack

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
